    "result": "Perfect! The bug is fixed. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Problem:** The `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file (`.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`) when run through the `frai` CLI, even though running `frai-gate init --ci` directly worked fine.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `frai` CLI's `gate` command was only passing positional arguments to the `frai-gate` subprocess via the `args` parameter. Commander.js separates positional arguments from flags, so the `--ci` flag was being dropped and never reached the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**Solution:** Modified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 752-753) to extract all arguments after the `gate` keyword from `process.argv` and pass those to the `frai-gate` CLI. This ensures that both positional arguments and flags are properly forwarded.\n\n**Verification:** Built the updated `frai-cli` package with `pnpm --filter frai build` and tested `frai gate init --ci` in a clean directory. Both the `FRAI-SPEC.md` template and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` workflow file are now successfully created.",
